  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D8">Default managed; unmanaged only when the intake says so. No environment-level or server-level default that flips it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="manifest contract">Manifest `solutions.SpaarkeMaster` = { version, managedBlobName, unmanagedBlobName }. A missing blob for the requested type → Resumable refusal naming the manifest; never fall back to the other type.</constraint>
    <constraint source="needed-or-remove">The catalog tiers, the retired-name guard (if only the catalog needs it), the PS importer options (SolutionPath, ImportMode) and Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 go unless something else reads them (grep first).</constraint>
    <constraint source="registry">Reuse an existing registry column or promotion path if one carries run parameters; a NEW Dataverse column on the admin registry is a live schema change — ask the owner first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">Real HTTP against hand-written handlers; never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;. The pac pre-import steps stay as they are (T253 owns them).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Intake: `solutionPackageType` (enum, default managed) in schema + catalog + endpoint, canonical on the run; parity tests.</step>
    <step order="2">H6/importer: one package; manifest schema with both blobs; pick by type; pre-check installed `solution` row (uniquename, version, ismanaged) → refuse type switch / downgrade; equal version → skip; verifier checks ismanaged; tests for every branch.</step>
    <step order="3">DAG `H9 ← H6`; DAG parity + run-context contract tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Registry: the package type and installed SpaarkeMaster version reach the registry row (existing path; ask before a new column).</step>
    <step order="5">Retire the catalog, Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 and its mirror test; skill Step 1 asks for the type only when the operator says unmanaged; guide + constraints.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify (ControlPlane tests, ArchTests, Worker + Api build 0 warnings); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">CreateRun: missing → managed; `unmanaged` accepted; any other value → 400; schema and endpoint agree.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H6 imports the managed blob by default and the unmanaged blob when asked; a manifest without the requested blob → Resumable refusal, no import call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Environment holds SpaarkeMaster of the other type → Resumable `solimport-package-type-mismatch` (or equivalent), no import; installed version higher → Resumable downgrade refusal, no import; equal → skip, success.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Verifier fails when the installed SpaarkeMaster's ismanaged differs from the requested type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DAG: H9 depends on H6; no cycle.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep` finds no CanonicalSolutionCatalog tier list, no Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 caller, and no "9 solutions" claim in src/ or scripts/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests and ArchTests pass; Worker/Api build with 0 warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Recording the type on the registry row needs a new admin-environment column (live schema change).</trigger>
    <trigger>Something outside H6 reads the catalog tiers or Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-07">COMPLETED (SESSION 43). Commits 3f41aab33 (implementation), 4f6c579ed (review fixes), d3aa70726 (re-check fixes). ControlPlane 2344/0 (1 skip), ArchTests 841/841, Worker/Api 0 warnings.
    - Intake solutionPackageType (managed | unmanaged, exact case; absent → managed stored at CreateRun; 400 intake-invalid-solution-package-type); schema + skill Step 1b-quinquies + Step 4.0; H6 declares it in HandlerRunInputs.
    - H6 imports ONE package (SpaarkePackage.SolutionUniqueName = SpaarkeMaster). Manifest {solutions:{SpaarkeMaster:{version, managedBlobName, unmanagedBlobName}}}; no fallback to the other type. Reads the installed row first (failure = failure, never "fresh"); refuses package-type-mismatch and downgrade-refused (Resumable, nothing imported); equal version (1.2 == 1.2.0.0) skips; a version that is not a version is refused.
    - REVIEW-DRIVEN: ImportSolutionAsync / StageAndUpgradeAsync (verified on Learn 2026-10-07) replace the synchronous actions, which held the request for the whole import and outlived the 100 s client timeout; completion = asyncoperations statecode 3 / statuscode 30, detail from importjobs.data; poll retries 404/401/408/429/5xx/transport/token errors until ImportTimeout with a fresh token per poll; PartialImport only for a managed StageAndUpgrade whose failure Dataverse reported; unmanaged update = ImportSolutionAsync. Verifier checks presence + ismanaged + version (Success carries the package version); an unreadable environment is Unavailable → verification-unavailable (Resumable), not a quarantine. Both named clients take DataverseWebApiRequestTimeout.
    - DAG H9 ← H6. sprk_solutionversion = "SpaarkeMaster {version} ({managed|unmanaged})" — records the package type on the registry row with no new column (supersedes owner D17's fingerprint; version-compatibility-matrix v3; skill Step 6a recomputes the same string).
    - Removed: CanonicalSolutionCatalog/ISolutionCatalog (9 entries, 6 never existed), DeployDataverseSolutionsScriptImporter, PacCliSolutionVerifier and their tests, PS-only options; retired-name guard (no catalog to scan; code kept [Obsolete] per the codes' stability rule).
    - DEVIATION (AC "no Deploy-DataverseSolutions.ps1 caller"): the script stays — Deploy-Release.ps1 (deploy-new-release skill, Spaarke's own environments) and the legacy Provision-Customer.ps1 still call it; H6 no longer does. Filed ISS-005 / #1401 (its list names 6 nonexistent solutions and its zip filter accepts every zip). Escalation trigger reported to the owner.
    - KNOWN LIMITS (K): a start POST that times out after Dataverse queued the job is reported as Timeout and resume is refused by "import already running" until it finishes (self-heals); a persistent 401/404 on the poll waits the full ImportTimeout; importer poll tests use real 80 ms deadlines; pre-import steps (required apps, org settings) run before the refusals (harmless — only raise values).</note>
  </notes>
</task>
